 ## Overview
-Rotated Halton Sampling is a stratified sampling technique that generates low-discrepancy Halton sequences for multiple dimensions while avoiding sequence correlation by rotating the sequence per stream and dimension [S1, unofficial]. It falls back to white noise for high dimensions [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Hammersley Sampling](8569-hammersley-sampling.md) by generalizing the radical inverse concept to arbitrary dimensions and introducing a rotation hash to decorrelate streams [S1, unofficial].
